{"kind":"finding","id":"F-trajectory-orbit-017-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/ReaimLoiterCompressorTests.cs","line":137,"method":"ComputeCuts_BodyChange_EndsRun","category":"T1","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Reaim/ReaimLoiterCompressor.cs:110; dropping next.bodyName != body leaves this GREEN; only raising aStepRelThreshold above 24285 -> red","what_it_asserts":"One cut starting at UT 0 when a Kerbin LKO loiter is followed by a 1 s Sun arc.","why_weak":"The Sun segment uses a=1.7e10 against LkoA=7e5, so the 5 percent a-step guard at line 115 ends the run before the body check matters; the body-change guard is unpinned.","proposed_action":"Give the second segment the SAME semiMajorAxis as the first and a duration of several of its own periods, so only the bodyName guard can end the run.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-trajectory-orbit-017-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/AnchorLifecycleTests.cs","line":69,"method":"IsAnchorLoaded_EmptyLoadedSet_AnchorNotFound_ReturnsFalse","category":"T2","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.WarpLoopPolicy.cs:805-815; invert either guard -> red in 8 tests at once","what_it_asserts":"Eight methods (lines 69, 77, 98, 162, 253, 263, 298, 332) re-assert the same three branches of a 12-line set-membership predicate.","why_weak":"IsAnchorLoaded is stateless and takes a uint, so Recording wrappers, multiple pids and add/remove sequences cannot reach new behavior; the file carries 15 methods for 3 branches.","proposed_action":"Collapse the eight into one Theory over (anchorPid, set contents, expected) plus the two log-line assertions already present at lines 43/52/61.","effort":"M","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-trajectory-orbit-017-03","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/TrajectoryWalkbackTests.cs","line":241,"method":"SimplePointToWorldPos_KnownPosition","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/SpawnCollisionDetector.cs:792-794; swap the y and z assignments -> stays GREEN; r = bodyRadius - pt.altitude -> red","what_it_asserts":"x=700000, y=0, z=0 for lat=0, lon=0, alt=100000 on a 600 km body.","why_weak":"lat=0 and lon=0 make both y and z zero, so axis swaps, lat/lon transposition and degree/radian sign errors all survive; only the radius+altitude term is pinned.","proposed_action":"Add one non-degenerate case (for example lat=30, lon=60) with independently computed x/y/z so the axis assignment and the degree-to-radian conversion are pinned.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-trajectory-orbit-017-04","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/TrajectoryWalkbackTests.cs","line":169,"method":"Walkback_FirstPointClear_ReturnsLastIndex","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/SpawnCollisionDetector.cs:464; start the loop at index 0 instead of Count-1 -> red","what_it_asserts":"Returns index 3 when only index 4 of a 5-point trajectory overlaps.","why_weak":"The name says the FIRST point is clear and the LAST index is returned; both halves are wrong for what the body sets up and asserts.","proposed_action":"Rename to Walkback_OnlyLastPointBlocked_ReturnsSecondToLastIndex.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-trajectory-orbit-017-05","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/AnchorLifecycleTests.cs","line":145,"method":"AnchoredLoop_AnchorNotLoaded_GhostSuppressed","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackLogic.WarpLoopPolicy.cs:814; return !loaded -> red","what_it_asserts":"IsAnchorLoaded returns false for an unloaded anchor pid.","why_weak":"The name claims the ghost is suppressed, but ShouldSpawnLoopedGhost (asserted in the sibling at line 123) is never called, so no suppression is observed.","proposed_action":"Either call ShouldSpawnLoopedGhost and assert the suppressed outcome, or rename to match the single predicate it checks.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
